From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Derumier <aderumier@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 05:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Drop an MPEG elementary stream picture the decoder
 rejects.

Without an FFmpeg MPEG video parser, transform_push_input() assembles
MPEG-1/2 elementary stream input into pictures itself. When
avcodec_send_packet() rejected a picture, it returned an error before
removing the picture from its buffer: every following input sent the
same picture again, which failed again, and the stream never recovered
(one "avcodec_send_packet" warning per input sample, no frame).

Drop the rejected picture and go on with the next one, the decoder
resynchronizes at the next decodable picture.
---
diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
index af6173d1..03e51cc2 100644
--- a/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/unix_transform.c
@@ -1279,8 +1279,9 @@ NTSTATUS transform_push_input( void *arg )
         if ((ret = avcodec_send_packet( t->avctx, t->parsed_packet )) < 0)
         {
             if (ret == AVERROR(EAGAIN)) return STATUS_DEVICE_BUSY;
-            WARN( "avcodec_send_packet: %d\n", ret );
-            return STATUS_UNSUCCESSFUL;
+            /* Drop the rejected picture: kept, it would be sent again with every input and
+             * fail for ever (e.g. a stream entered without its sequence header). */
+            WARN( "avcodec_send_packet: %d, dropping %u bytes\n", ret, next_pic );
         }
 
         memmove( t->mpeg_es_buf, t->mpeg_es_buf + next_pic, t->mpeg_es_size - next_pic );
